@page "/examples/editable-node"

<PageTitle>Editable Node · Blow</PageTitle>

<ExampleScaffold Title="Editable Node"
                 Summary="Nodes can host real form controls. Typing in a field - Backspace and Delete included - edits the text and leaves the graph alone, because the canvas ignores its keys while focus is in an editable element; a drag handle keeps the fields usable by leaving the rest of the node undraggable.">
    <ChildContent>
        <BlowCanvas Nodes="_nodes" Edges="_edges" FitViewOnInit="true">
            <NodeTemplate Context="node">
                <BlowHandle Type="BlowHandleType.Target" Position="BlowPosition.Top" />
                <div class="edit-node">
                    <BlowDragHandle Class="edit-grip">⠿ @node.Id</BlowDragHandle>
                    <input class="edit-input"
                           aria-label="@($"Label of {node.Id}")"
                           value="@node.Label"
                           @oninput="@(e => node.Label = e.Value?.ToString())" />
                    <textarea class="edit-notes"
                              aria-label="@($"Notes on {node.Id}")"
                              placeholder="notes…"
                              @oninput="@(e => SetNotes(node, e.Value?.ToString()))">@Notes(node)</textarea>
                </div>
                <BlowHandle Type="BlowHandleType.Source" Position="BlowPosition.Bottom" />
            </NodeTemplate>
            <ChildContent>
                <BlowBackground Variant="BlowBackgroundVariant.Lines" Gap="24" Color="var(--bit-blow-border)" />
                <BlowControls />
            </ChildContent>
        </BlowCanvas>
    </ChildContent>
    <TryIt>
        <li><strong>Click into a label field</strong> and type, using <strong>Backspace</strong> and <strong>Delete</strong> freely: the text changes and the node stays.</li>
        <li><strong>Write in a notes box</strong>: a textarea is just as safe.</li>
        <li><strong>Drag a node by its grip</strong> (⠿ and its id) to move it. Pressing or dragging in the fields never moves it.</li>
        <li>To delete a node, <strong>click its grip</strong> - that selects the node and takes focus out of the fields - then press <strong>Delete</strong> or <strong>Backspace</strong>.</li>
    </TryIt>
    <HowItWorks>
        <li>Graph keys - Delete, Backspace, the arrows, Ctrl+A - are ignored while focus is in a text input, textarea, select or contenteditable element, so a field inside a node is safe to type in. Escape still abandons a gesture in progress.</li>
        <li>Pressing a field still selects its node; it is the focus in the field that keeps Delete from removing it.</li>
        <li><code>UseCustomDragHandle = true</code> stops the node's body from starting a drag, and the <code>BlowDragHandle</code> grip starts one instead - so placing the caret or selecting text never moves the node.</li>
        <li>The label field writes to <code>node.Label</code> on every keystroke, and <code>Label</code> is also the node's accessible name. The notes live in a dictionary on the page, keyed by node id.</li>
        <li>The other way to hand a field its presses back is the <code>nodrag</code> class (the canvas's <code>NoDragClass</code>) on the field itself, which leaves the rest of the body draggable; the Custom Node example does that.</li>
    </HowItWorks>
</ExampleScaffold>

<style>
    .edit-node { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; width: 190px; padding: 2px; text-align: left; }
    /* The canvas's own --bit-blow-* colours, so the fields follow its colour mode. */
    .edit-grip { padding: 2px 4px; font-size: 10px; color: var(--bit-blow-text-muted); border-radius: 4px; background: var(--bit-blow-surface-muted); }
    .edit-input { width: 100%; padding: 4px 6px; font: inherit; color: var(--bit-blow-text); background: var(--bit-blow-surface); border: 1px solid var(--bit-blow-border); border-radius: 4px; }
    .edit-notes { width: 100%; height: 48px; padding: 4px 6px; font: inherit; resize: none; color: var(--bit-blow-text); background: var(--bit-blow-surface); border: 1px solid var(--bit-blow-border); border-radius: 4px; }
</style>

@code {
    private readonly Dictionary<string, string> _notes = [];

    private List<BlowNode> _nodes = [];
    private List<BlowEdge> _edges = [];

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        // UseCustomDragHandle keeps the text fields usable: only the grip starts a drag.
        _nodes =
        [
            new BlowNode { Id = "1", Label = "Collect input", Position = new(0, 0), UseCustomDragHandle = true },
            new BlowNode { Id = "2", Label = "Transform", Position = new(280, 60), UseCustomDragHandle = true },
        ];

        _edges = [new BlowEdge { Id = "e1-2", Source = "1", Target = "2", Animated = true }];
    }

    private string Notes(BlowNode node) => _notes.GetValueOrDefault(node.Id, string.Empty);

    private void SetNotes(BlowNode node, string? value) => _notes[node.Id] = value ?? string.Empty;
}
